                <pb facs="1315" n="1305" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5034 Registration/3–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in China
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-03-14T21:00:00-05:00">March 14, 1946—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>469. American business interests are in quandary as to what is present status of
                    revised company law, and whether registration is required prior to March 31, and
                    if so under what law. Dr. Robert Huang, attorney for China-America Council is of
                    opinion, as is Chinese Embassy, he reports, that registration requirement prior
                    to March 31 is under “Regulations for Registration of Companies,” June 9, 1943.
                    Commerce requests clarification.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
